        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Garage floor crack repair before a coating comes down to sorting. Dormant cracks get chased, filled with a rigid epoxy or polyurea filler and ground perfectly flush. Control joints and moving cracks get flexible treatment or are left as joints. Damp slabs get fixed or primed with a moisture-tolerant product before anything else.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Do those three things and the cracks disappear under the new floor and stay gone. Skip them and the coating will show you exactly where every crack was, usually within the first winter.
          </p>
